.TH SINH 3 "2026-05-03" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
sinh, sinhf, sinhl, cosh, coshf, coshl, tanh, tanhf, tanhl \- hyperbolic functions
.SH LIBRARY
Math library (libm, \-lm)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.BI "double sinh(double " x );
.br
.BI "float sinhf(float " x );
.br
.BI "long double sinhl(long double " x );
.PP
.BI "double cosh(double " x );
.br
.BI "float coshf(float " x );
.br
.BI "long double coshl(long double " x );
.PP
.BI "double tanh(double " x );
.br
.BI "float tanhf(float " x );
.br
.BI "long double tanhl(long double " x );
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR sinh ()
function returns the hyperbolic sine of
.IR x ,
defined mathematically as
.RI ( e^x \ \-\ e^-x )/2 .
It is an odd function whose domain is the entire real line and whose
range is also the entire real line.
.PP
The
.BR cosh ()
function returns the hyperbolic cosine of
.IR x ,
defined mathematically as
.RI ( e^x \ +\ e^-x )/2 .
It is an even function whose domain is the entire real line and whose
range is the half-open interval
.BR [1,\ +\[if]) .
.PP
The
.BR tanh ()
function returns the hyperbolic tangent of
.IR x ,
defined mathematically as
.IR sinh( x )/ cosh( x ) .
It is an odd function whose domain is the entire real line and whose
range is the open interval
.BR (\-1,\ +1) ,
with horizontal asymptotes at \(+-1 as
.I x
tends to \(+-\[if].
.PP
The
.BR sinhf (),
.BR coshf (),
and
.BR tanhf ()
variants take and return
.B float
values.  The
.BR sinhl (),
.BR coshl (),
and
.BR tanhl ()
variants take and return
.B "long double"
values.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, these functions return the hyperbolic value of
.I x
as described above.
.PP
If
.I x
is +0 (\-0), all three functions return +0 (\-0).
.PP
If
.I x
is positive infinity,
.BR sinh ()
returns positive infinity,
.BR cosh ()
returns positive infinity, and
.BR tanh ()
returns +1.  If
.I x
is negative infinity,
.BR sinh ()
returns negative infinity,
.BR cosh ()
returns positive infinity, and
.BR tanh ()
returns \-1.
.PP
If
.I x
is a NaN, all three functions return a NaN.
.PP
If the magnitude of the result of
.BR sinh ()
or
.BR cosh ()
is too large to be representable in the return type, a range
(overflow) error occurs and the function returns
.B \(+-HUGE_VAL
(or
.B \(+-HUGE_VALF
or
.BR \(+-HUGE_VALL )
with the appropriate sign.
.PP
.BR tanh ()
never overflows; its result always lies in
.BR (\-1,\ +1) .
.SH ERRORS
See
.BR math_error (7)
for information on how to determine whether an error has occurred when
calling these functions.
.PP
The following errors can occur:
.TP
Range error: result overflow (\fBsinh\fR, \fBcosh\fR)
An overflow floating-point exception
.RB ( FE_OVERFLOW )
is raised.  If
.I "math_errhandling & MATH_ERRNO"
is non-zero,
.I errno
is set to
.BR ERANGE .
.PP
.BR tanh ()
does not raise range errors for any finite or infinite argument.
.SH ATTRIBUTES
For an explanation of the terms used in this section, see
.BR attributes (7).
.TS
allbox;
lb lb lb
l l l.
Interface	Attribute	Value
T{
.BR sinh (),
.BR sinhf (),
.BR sinhl (),
.BR cosh (),
.BR coshf (),
