.BR tanhf (),
.BR tanhl ()
T}	Thread safety	MT-Safe
.TE
.SH STANDARDS
.BR sinh (),
.BR cosh (),
.BR tanh (),
and their
.BR f / l
variants conform to C99 and POSIX.1-2008.  The handling of special
arguments follows C99 Annex F.10.2 (IEC 60559).
.SH EXAMPLES
The following program computes the hyperbolic sine, cosine, and
tangent of 1.0:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
#include <math.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int
main(void)
{
    double x = 1.0;

    printf("sinh(%.6f) = %.6f\en", x, sinh(x));
    printf("cosh(%.6f) = %.6f\en", x, cosh(x));
    printf("tanh(%.6f) = %.6f\en", x, tanh(x));
    return 0;
}
.EE
.RE
